from ./Access import Access
from ./Email import Email

export anchor StoredWork:
    what:
        The application stores the work a person made while a project
        exists, so a person can come back to it in the same browser or on
        any device they sign in on.
    stored:
        - The company description and the other inputs of each project
        - The style choices of each project
        - Every candidate, with its reason, style tag and domain status
        - The names the person rejected
        - The notes the person wrote
        - The usage spent on each project
        - The account, plan, credits and seats, and the counters of the allowance
    notStored:
        - Card numbers or any payment detail, which stay with the payment provider
        - A password in readable form; only a one-way hash is kept
        - The text of a message in flight inside the model prompt after the round ends
        - A network address in readable form; only a one-way hash is kept for the month
    anonymous:
        Work made with no account lives in the browser. It is reachable
        only from that browser until the person signs in, and signing in
        attaches it to the account under @{Access}.
    scope:
        One project's work is readable only by the people who may see it.
        Those people are its owner, the members of an organization it is
        shared with, and the operator for support. No other person and no
        other project can reach it.

export anchor Export:
    meaning:
        A person can take their work out as a file at any time, with no
        support request.
    formats:
        - A spreadsheet-ready file of the candidate list, with name, reason, style and domain status
        - A plain text list of names, one per line
    rules:
        - Export covers one project or every project the person can see
        - An export of a shared project includes who added each name
        - Export never needs a payment, and stays available when the allowance is used up
        - A person who has no account can export the project in the browser
        - Copying a shortlist to the clipboard gives the same plain text list

export anchor Deletion:
    meaning:
        A person can delete a project or an account at any time, and
        deletion is the only thing that removes the work.
    project:
        Deleting a project removes its description, candidates, rejected
        names, notes and usage record from the live system at once. It
        disappears from every view, including the view of another member of
        a shared project.
    account:
        Deleting an account removes its projects, its counters and its
        sign-in. Any organization the person owns must be closed or handed
        to another member first, and the person is told which.
    grace:
        A deleted account is kept for 30 days and then dropped. During
        those 30 days the person can sign in and restore it in full. After
        30 days nothing is kept and the work cannot be restored.
    backups:
        A copy in a backup is dropped within the same 30-day window, so no
        deleted work outlives the grace period in any copy.
    notice:
        Before an account is deleted the person is told what will be
        removed and when. A deletion is confirmed by email once it happens,
        under @{Email}.
    others:
        Deleting a project never removes another member's account. Closing
        an organization never deletes the personal accounts of its members.
